      "body": "NPU GPTQ linear layers produce incorrect outputs when the zero point differs from the signed-weight midpoint. For example, a 4-bit layer with weight 10, zero point 9, scale 0.5 and 256 unit inputs returns 384 instead of 128.\n\nThe loader shifts both weights and zero points by the midpoint. `npu_weight_quant_batchmatmul` adds `antiquant_offset`, so the converted zero point needs to be negated. Do this once during weight loading, after the GPTQ v1 `+1` adjustment. Symmetric zero points remain zero.\n\nTested the original and patched loader/matmul on Ascend NPU with torch-npu 2.10.0.post6: 4/8-bit, GPTQ v1/v2, FP16/BF16, symmetric/asymmetric and boundary zero points, random weights, group sizes 64/128, bias, and 2D/3D inputs. Before: 8 passed, 48 failed. After: 56 passed. Reference is FP32 dequantization/matmul cast to the output dtype (`rtol=0.02, atol=0.125`). This is a kernel-level check, not a full-model accuracy run.\n\n[Per-case results](https://github.com/AkiYangDev/sglang/blob/789468d8b4a2fc3fc664a67535d27c3271e057f5/RESULT.json). The screenshot below renders those saved results.\n\n![NPU GPTQ validation](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/AkiYangDev/sglang@789468d8b4a2fc3fc664a67535d27c3271e057f5/validation.png)\n\nFormatting/lint checks passed. Two pre-commit hooks could not resolve `python3` on Windows; both scripts passed when run directly with the installed Python.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41190481338](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41190481338)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41190481310](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41190481310)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41190481365](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41190481365)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
